---
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, getPage } from "../lib/site";

const page = getPage("/terms");
---
<Base title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path}>
  <PageHead
    title="Terms of use"
    lead="These terms cover kalcoded.com, the KalCode early-access list and the KalCode preview app."
  >
    <p class="muted small">Last updated September 24, 2026</p>
  </PageHead>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
      <p>
        By using kalcoded.com (the “site”), joining the early-access list, or downloading, installing
        or using the KalCode desktop app (the “app”), you agree to these terms. If you do not agree,
        please do not use the site or the app.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The site</h2>
      <p>
        The site describes KalCode, a product in early preview. Descriptions of features, plans and
        prices reflect current plans and may change. Nothing on the site is an offer to sell, and no
        purchase can be made through it today.
      </p>
      <p>
        KalCode is designed to work with AI providers through your own accounts. Your use of a
        provider is governed by your agreement with that provider and billed by it; KalCode does
        not sell, resell or meter provider usage.
      </p>

      <h2 id="preview">3. The KalCode preview app</h2>
      <p>
        The app is currently offered as a free preview. These terms apply to every preview version
        until a version comes with terms of its own.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Licence.</strong> We give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
          revocable licence to download, install and use the app on computers you control, for your
          own work, including work for your employer or clients. KalCode and the app remain ours;
          all rights not granted here are reserved.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Restrictions.</strong> Do not sell, rent, redistribute or publicly host the app or
          its installer, remove its notices, or reverse engineer it except where the law allows this
          despite these terms. Share the download link instead.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your work and your providers.</strong> The app runs on your computer. Your code,
          projects and data stay yours, and we do not receive them. AI providers you connect run on
          your own accounts; your use of them is governed by your agreements with those providers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your decisions.</strong> The app can run coding agents and commands in your projects
          within the permission mode you choose. You are responsible for the modes you select, the
          actions you approve and for reviewing changes before you rely on them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Preview quality.</strong> Preview versions are incomplete, may contain errors, may
          change or remove features, and are not code-signed yet. Keep backups of work that matters,
          including your projects under version control.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ending use.</strong> You may stop at any time by uninstalling the app. We may end a
          preview; the licence for that version then ends and you should uninstall it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. The early-access list</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Joining is free and requires only an email address that you are entitled to use, confirmed
          from the email we send to it.
        </li>
        <li>
          Joining does not guarantee access to any build, on any date, and does not create an
          account or any other obligation for you or for us.
        </li>
        <li>
          We will use your address only as described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>.
          You can remove it at any time on that page.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>submit an email address that is not yours, or submit addresses in bulk;</li>
        <li>attempt to disrupt, overload, probe or bypass the security of the site or its API;</li>
        <li>scrape the site in a way that degrades it for others;</li>
        <li>use the site to break any law.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Names and marks</h2>
      <p>
        KalCode, KalVoice, the KalCode wordmark, the KalCode symbol and the KalVoice orb are
        ours. You may not use them in a way that suggests endorsement or affiliation
        without permission. Claude Code, Codex and Gemini CLI are products and trademarks of their
        respective owners; naming them describes compatibility and does not imply endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2>7. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site and the app are provided “as is” and “as available”. To the extent the law allows,
        we make no warranties about them, express or implied, including fitness for a particular
        purpose, that they will be uninterrupted or error-free, that code or changes produced with
        the app are correct, or that KalCode will be offered in any particular form or on any
        particular date.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental or
        consequential loss, or for loss of data, code or profits, arising from your use of the site,
        the early-access list or the app. Nothing in
        these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. When we do, we will change the date at the top of this page.
        Continuing to use the site after an update means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms, or legal and privacy requests:
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. You can also remove
        your email address at any time with the form on the <a href="/privacy#remove">privacy page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
